The Seals must be fitted to the following components at all times:

Left valve cover;

Right valve cover;

Oil sump;

Side throttle body (left);

Side throttle body (right);

Connector for ECU wiring harness (2 Seals); and

Gearbox housing and differential cover (2 Seals)

At the sole discretion of the TD , an Automobile or component thereof may be sealed by the TD for examination at a later date.

It is the Competitor's responsibility to ensure that each component that is required to be sealed is done so by the correct authority prior to the first Round in which the Automobile competes .

Unless otherwise approved in writing by the TD or TM , each sealed component must remain sealed until removed in accordance with Regulation T2.4.5.

Unless otherwise approved in writing by the TD or TM , a Seal is only permitted to be removed by the TD , TM , or the specified Control Component Service Agent as nominated by the CM .

If written approval is given by the TD or TM for a Seal to be removed by someone other than those nominated in Regulation T2.4.5, the component is only permitted to be re-sealed by the TD , the TM or their nominee.

